{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789416228,"nonce":"i6d2fsL5hpO/Ugnn3Xwd7blx5yM=","title":"CI: the Windows native tests hang in bench_memory_probe","message":"Since 824c978 made the runtime's symbols reach the interpreter on\nWindows, the ZynML benchmark kernels run there for the first time in\nCI, and `crates/zynml/tests/bench_memory_probe.rs` (both tests) never\nreturned: run 34852351972's Windows job sat in that binary from 14:05\nuntil the six-hour limit cancelled it at 19:57. Linux and macOS finish\nthe same tests in under a minute. Earlier Windows runs never reached\nthe kernels (compile errors, then the symbol error), so this is not a\nregression of the probe but the first time the kernels have run on\nthat target.\n\nThe probe now writes each kernel's name straight to stderr before\nrunning it, past the harness capture, so the next Windows run names\nthe kernel that does not return; the job has a two-hour limit. Once\nthe kernel is known: run it alone on Windows with `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1`\nand `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_INTERP_OPTS=1` to split the JIT, the OSR transfer\nand the passes.","files":null}]}